<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Forty Years' War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1385–1424</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Forty Years' War was a series of campaigns between the Burmese-speaking Ava Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burma">Upper Burma</a> and the Mon-speaking Hanthawaddy Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burma">Lower Burma</a>. Ava's kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swa-saw-ke">Swa Saw Ke</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minkhaung-i">Minkhaung I</a> tried repeatedly to conquer the south, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/razadarit">Razadarit</a> of Hanthawaddy held them off and raided north. Neither side prevailed, and the two kingdoms remained separate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/forty-years-war.jpg" alt="Forty Years' War" width="320" height="634" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hybernator · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burma_in_1450.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
